      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "My apologies for the confusion. Here's the technical information you need for the ARIA roles for a transaction history list:\n\n1. ARIA Role for Transaction History List: Use the `role=\"list\"` attribute to indicate that the element is a list. This helps screen readers understand that the content is a list of items.\n\n2. ARIA Role for Each Transaction Item: Apply the `role=\"listitem\"` attribute to each individual transaction within the list. This informs screen readers that each item is a part of the list.\n\n3. ARIA Role for the List Container: If the transaction history is within a specific container, such as a div or section, you can use `role=\"list\"` on the container itself to provide context to screen reader users.\n\n4. ARIA Role for the Transaction Details: For each transaction, you may also want to use `role=\"grid\"` or `role=\"tree\"` if the transaction details are presented in a grid or hierarchical structure, respectively. This helps screen readers understand the layout and navigate through the details more effectively.\n\n5. ARIA Role for the Transaction Summary: If there is a summary or summary section for the transaction history, use `role=\"region\"` or `role=\"complementary\"`",
      "source": "target",
